// Debug signing entry point — TRACKED and committed.
//
// This file exists so `project.yml`'s `configFiles` reference is always
// valid (xcodegen fails spec validation if the referenced xcconfig is
// missing, which would break CI). It is otherwise a no-op.
//
// WHY YOU WANT THE OPTIONAL OVERRIDE BELOW
// Without a stable signing identity the Debug build is ad-hoc signed, and
// ad-hoc signing produces a new code hash on every build. macOS TCC keys
// permission grants (Accessibility, Microphone) to that identity, so every
// rebuild looks like a new app and your granted permissions are dropped.
//
// TO FIX LOCALLY (per developer)
//   1. Find your Apple Development cert's SHA-1:
//          security find-identity -v -p codesigning
//   2. Create `Local.private.xcconfig` (gitignored) with:
//          CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
//          CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = <your-cert-SHA-1>
//
// SCOPE: Debug/local only. Release signing and notarization are handled by
// Tools/packaging and are unaffected. If the private file is absent (e.g. on
// CI), the optional include below is a no-op and the ad-hoc default stands.
#include? "Local.private.xcconfig"

// Per-developer Debug-only feature flag overrides, same pattern as the
// signing override above: gitignored and OSS-excluded, so this is a no-op
// everywhere except a developer machine that has deliberately created the
// file. See project.yml's INTERNAL_INTERACTIVE_AUTH_CONDITION build setting
// for the single flag this currently exists to set.
#include? "Local.internal.xcconfig"
